  "final_answer": "r prunes.\n\n**Gate that failed:** `main` is checked out only in a prunable worktree entry. `git worktree list --porcelain` shows `<root>/wt-main` on `refs/heads/main` (`a7865db`) with \"gitdir file points to non-existent location\". The command stops on this even for a preview. The skill forbids a repository-wide `git worktree prune`, because it would also drop other entries.\n\n**What I saw:**\n- **Invoking worktree:** the repo root, on `agent/release` (`724a44b`). It is clean.\n- **Target:** `agent/release` has no upstream.\n- **Other local branches:**\n  - `main` (`a7865db`) tracks `origin/main`.\n  - `agent/a` (`8eccc62`) has no upstream and no worktree entry of its own.\n- **Not evaluated:** I didn't compute the plan (unique commits, `PREDICTED_CONFLICT` hints) because the gate failed first.\n\n**To unblock it:** clear the stale `wt-main` entry yourself, then rerun. Either of these works:\n- If the directory is gone for good, run `git worktree prune`. You have to run it, since I won't. It only drops entries whose directory is missing, and `wt-main` is the only entry besides the repo root.\n- If you moved the directory, run `git worktree repair <new-path>` instead.\n\nOnce `main` is no longer tied to a prunable entry, I can run the preview and then the apply. Expected result: `main` and `agent/a` get merged into `agent/release`, then `agent/a` is deleted, leaving only `main` and `agent/release`. The remote branches would not have the merged commits.",
